WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I spoke to many of these
Muslim, former Muslim,

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.208
agnostic Muslim,
moderate Muslim,

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.977
whatever you want to
call them, guys saying,

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:16.549
"If we don't take the lead
in breaking this thing open,

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:21.654 align:start size:97% position:3%
"the countries that we have
fled to are going to look like

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.590
"the countries we fled from."

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.493
(calm theme music)

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.098 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.134 line:0%
is a human rights activist,

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:37.470 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
a fellow at Stanford
University's Hoover Institute,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.339 align:start size:84% position:16%
a best-selling author
whose new book,

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.808
"Prey: Immigration, Islam,

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:46.146
"and the Erosion of Women's
Rights" is out right now.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:48.848
Ayaan Hirsi Ali, welcome
back to "The Rubin Report."

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.383
- Thank you so much, David.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.618
Thank you for having me on.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:52.919 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I'm thrilled
to have you on.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.055
We were just discussing
right before we started,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.589
we've done this a couple times.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.458
We'd prefer to do it in person,

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:01.795
but we are left to
the wires of Skype.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:03.596
So I wanna talk about
the book, obviously,

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.231
and that's what we're
mostly gonna do today.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.901
But since I haven't chatted
with you, at least publicly,

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:11.271
in about a year, how's
the year been for you?

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.705
How are you doing?

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.707 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
What do you make of the state
of the world, my friend?

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:20.146 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- Well, it's
different, isn't it?

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.350
And that's obviously
an understatement.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.653 align:start size:81% position:19%
I belong to the
category of people

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
for whom COVID has
actually been a good thing

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.327
in the sense that I can be
very close to my family.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:37.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I have never been
more productive in my life

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:41.367 align:start size:88% position:13%
because we've killed
the commute time, right?

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.103
We are not going to the office.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:47.941
We are not commuting to
the places where I speak.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.376
You know, it would take
me at least three days

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.078
to give one single speech,

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:56.082
and now it's Zoom
calls back to back.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.550
That's the nature of our life.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:03.256
But again, having said that,
I know that there are millions

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:07.694
and millions of people whose
livelihoods are compromised.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:08.895
That's really sad.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.701
A lot of societies have
cracked their economies.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.106
People are going through all
sorts of mental health issues.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.876
Domestic violence has gone up,

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.713 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I couldn't wait
for this thing to end.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.148
I hate COVID.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Are you shocked, even
though it's been okay for you,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.455
and truth be told, in terms
of my life and my businesses,

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:38.124
it's been okay for me, but
obviously there's all sorts

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.860 align:start size:97% position:3%
of horrific stuff happening,
as you're addressing.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
Are you shocked,
though, how quickly,

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
as someone that comes from
a not very free place,

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:49.969
and I think most of my audience
is familiar with your story,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.739 align:start size:84% position:16%
are you shocked how
quickly we in the West

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.241
are willing to give up
our rights and freedoms?

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.714
- I don't know if the
word to use is shock.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think the word
that I would use now

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.787 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's in the beginning, we
didn't know what was going on.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.689 align:start size:84% position:16%
This could have been
the Spanish flu.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.991
It could have been smallpox,

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.893 align:start size:88% position:13%
it could have been
tuberculosis, and again,

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.095
because I do come from Africa,

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.866 align:start size:97% position:3%
I do come from societies
where large numbers of people

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:23.336
are killed by pandemics,

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.905 align:start size:84% position:16%
many of them children
and the young.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
Obviously, in the
beginning, I was really

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.978 align:start size:84% position:16%
really frightened
like everybody else.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then the more we find
out about the disease

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:39.919 align:start size:97% position:3%
the more I think our response,
at times, is politicized,

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:45.525
it's overwrought, in some
ways it's exaggerated.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.861 align:start size:84% position:16%
But what really
bothers me the most

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:52.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that we can't even
have these conversations.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:55.168 align:start size:84% position:16%
That if you say, maybe
like my colleague

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:59.372 align:start position:0%
at the Hoover Institution,
Scott Atlas, who's a scientist,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:03.009
and if he comes out and he
says, and along with him,

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:06.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
many others who say, "Wait
a second, let's reflect

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:10.650
"on these trade-offs," that
these people are demonized.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.419 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's what bothers me the
most, because I don't think

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:17.290
that the virus cares if
you're black or white,

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:21.594
rich or poor, religious
or not, they don't care.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.297
The virus doesn't care
about your politics.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:28.568
And so I think maybe to
use the word shocking

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:31.137
is that I thought
liberal societies

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:35.208 align:start size:88% position:13%
were rational societies
guided by reason.

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.510
And right now we're
going through a time

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:41.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
when reason is not the
prevailing characteristic.

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.849
And that is unfortunate.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:45.518 align:start size:97% position:3%
- That's exactly what I wanted
to ask you next, actually,

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:49.289
because you were gracious
enough to give me a quote

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:52.091 align:start size:88% position:13%
on classical
liberalism for my book.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think you've been
one of the great defenders

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.329
of classical liberalism,
not only intellectually,

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.032 align:start size:88% position:13%
but also just by
extension of your life.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.333
But what I'm seeing right now,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.101 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I think this is
what you're hitting on,

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.470 align:start size:84% position:16%
it seems to me we're
almost at the end

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.406
of Western liberalism.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:09.976
That sort of the woke-ism and
the giant government stuff

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:14.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
has basically
enveloped liberalism,

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.983
and in essence, the good
few remaining liberals

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:81% position:19%
are sort of modern
conservatives.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.820
That actually what
I consider myself,

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I would've never
said that three years ago.

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you think that's
a fair summary?

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:30.029
- I think that if you go
to a place where you saying

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:35.968
"There is no hope, we're
going to self-destruct,"

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.874
then I caution you on that,

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.377
and say we have had times

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:47.680 align:start size:97% position:3%
when we were just this
divided and really irrational.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
So again, I'm with people
like Steve Pinker on,

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:54.921
actually things haven't
been better for humanity.

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:59.559
If you take that long,
long trajectory from when

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:03.696
we stopped walking on all fours
and started walking upright.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.164
- Yeah, yeah, no.

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I know that, of
course things are better.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.167
I've read the book.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.769
I think I've got it back here.

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:11.938
You know, Pinker's book
"Enlightenment Now."

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:15.575 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I know things
actually aren't that bad

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:16.809 align:start size:88% position:13%
although we've got a
certain set of problems,

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:19.779
but I do sense that
liberalism itself

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.814 align:start size:84% position:16%
seems to be being
destroyed right now,

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:26.052 align:start size:97% position:3%
that woke-ism has destroyed,
at the academic level,

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:28.087 align:start size:88% position:13%
what you're seeing at
all of the institutions,

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:31.391
that liberalism is in a
particularly tough spot.

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:34.260
- You are absolutely right.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.129
Liberalism, by the way,

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:43.503
I'd say it's probably one of
the youngest of philosophies,

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:48.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
classical liberalism,
and from the time

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:51.177
that the Enlightenment and
classical liberalism emerged,

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:53.780
it has always been under threat.

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:58.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's this
beautiful golden age time

00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:01.888
when it triumphed.

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:06.125
But that triumph was, it
was like a back and forth.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:11.564
You know, we only had the
First and Second World Wars

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:14.767
in the 20th century, right?

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:18.070
In that century,
when things seem,

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.506
people seemed to be
attracted to reason.

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:23.376
And I think this is
not going to stop.

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:26.646
Liberalism is once
again, challenged.

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, obviously, I was
really very much engaged,

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.484
as you know, from my background,

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:36.489
with the challenges that
political Islam presents.

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:39.425
The narrative of
political Islam is

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:42.795
liberalism is wrong,
individualism is wrong,

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.263
universalism is wrong.

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:47.700 align:start size:97% position:3%
And only the way they see
and the utopia of their goals

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.703
is the right way, and that
the way you achieve that

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:53.773
is through violence,
through sacrifice,

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:58.778
through misogyny, and through
all sorts of other affronts

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:01.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the idea and
philosophy of liberalism.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:04.884
Now what's interesting
with the woke ideology

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:09.555
is that it is actually a
byproduct of liberalism,

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:13.326 align:start size:97% position:3%
that it is a disappointment
with the world.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:16.329 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so if you read that
book, I sent it to everybody

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:18.564
I could send it to,
"Cynical Theories"-

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:19.599
- I have it.

00:08:19.599 --> 00:08:20.800
I've had James on, yeah.

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:25.905
- To, I would say, modern day
liberals, Helen Pluckrose,

00:08:25.905 --> 00:08:27.540
and James Lindsay.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.543
What they're trying
to show us is that

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:32.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you dig deep, and
that's what they've done,

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:36.182 align:start size:88% position:13%
dig deep into the
philosophies that inform

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:40.152 align:start position:0%
what we now call woke-ism,
cancel culture, critical theory,

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:42.655
critical race theory,
it goes by many names,

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.492 align:start size:84% position:16%
but that is an
unintended consequence

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:49.695 align:start size:97% position:3%
of liberalism disappointment
with modernity.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:52.999
It's a disappointment
with civilization.

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:56.402
It's a yearning for
some kind of utopia.

00:08:56.402 --> 00:09:01.340 align:start size:97% position:3%
It does use secular
arguments and underpinnings,

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:05.912 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it does have a
religious quality to it.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.619 line:0%
I've compared it
with radical Islam.

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:17.857 line:0%
You know, they want to
shut down free inquiry.

00:09:17.857 --> 00:09:20.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have those who are
in, and those who are out.

00:09:22.328 --> 00:09:25.765
They don't want to have
a conversation with you,

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:27.833
they want to destroy you.

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:32.838 align:start size:88% position:13%
They divide society
into subsets of groups.

00:09:33.706 --> 00:09:35.441
They deny objective truth.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:37.443
They're hostile to science.

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:41.948 align:start size:97% position:3%
Hey, by the way, they say
they're standing up for women,

00:09:41.948 --> 00:09:44.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
and gays, and transgender
people, and so on,

00:09:44.417 --> 00:09:46.719
but if you look at
what they're saying

00:09:46.719 --> 00:09:48.487
they're actually
the most racist,

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:51.390 align:start size:84% position:16%
misogynistic people
in the world.

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.225
And so in that sense

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:56.295
I would say here's a new
challenge to liberalism.

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:57.697
It shouldn't surprise us.

00:09:57.697 --> 00:09:59.532
If you're a true
classical liberal,

00:09:59.532 --> 00:10:04.503 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know that the
challenges, ideological,

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.272 align:start size:84% position:16%
philosophical
challenges to liberal

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.507
they're commonplace and
they'll stay with us,

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:11.544
because that's what
human nature demands.

00:10:12.979 --> 00:10:16.315
And so that's why I don't
want us to go to a place

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:19.719
where we are saying this
is the end of liberalism,

00:10:19.719 --> 00:10:21.520
or the end of free society.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:26.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we should just,
how else, it's like aging.

00:10:28.594 --> 00:10:31.230 align:start size:84% position:16%
Liberalism will
forever be challenged.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:36.202
We just have to be aware
and conscious of that.

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:39.005 align:start size:84% position:16%
And even after radical
Islam is defeated,

00:10:39.005 --> 00:10:40.573
woke-ism is defeated,

00:10:42.008 --> 00:10:44.377 align:start size:88% position:13%
like national
socialism was defeated,

00:10:44.377 --> 00:10:46.445 align:start size:84% position:16%
and all sorts of
other fascistic ideas,

00:10:46.445 --> 00:10:47.713
but it's not going to go away.

00:10:47.713 --> 00:10:52.618 align:start size:84% position:16%
Something is gonna
come in a new disguise

00:10:52.618 --> 00:10:54.153
that will be new to the people

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:55.688
who will be living
through that time.

00:10:55.688 --> 00:10:56.822
- Yeah.

00:10:56.822 --> 00:10:58.124 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, it's
interesting when I talk

00:10:58.124 --> 00:11:00.026
about sort of the end of
the road for liberalism,

00:11:00.026 --> 00:11:03.162
what it means to me
is that now I feel

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:06.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I can do much more
work helping to liberalize

00:11:06.632 --> 00:11:08.934 align:start size:84% position:16%
or even use some
libertarian principles

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:10.870
with my conservative friends.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.939 align:start size:97% position:3%
That seems like a smart
place to put energy for me,

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:17.877
as opposed to trying to fix
the woke part of this thing.

00:11:17.877 --> 00:11:20.813
But I think this is
the challenge for
all of the liberals

00:11:20.813 --> 00:11:23.182
at the moment is sort
of which way do you go?

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:24.984
- Which way do you go?

00:11:24.984 --> 00:11:26.218
Well, what I'm saying is yes,

00:11:26.218 --> 00:11:28.921 align:start size:84% position:16%
you have to find
allies and alliances.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:33.192
So first of all, we
have to go back to

00:11:33.192 --> 00:11:38.197 align:start size:84% position:16%
Americans call
classical liberalism,

00:11:39.565 --> 00:11:40.966
they call it conservatism.

00:11:42.501 --> 00:11:44.203
The Europeans just
call it liberalism

00:11:44.203 --> 00:11:46.839 align:start size:84% position:16%
because that's where
it all emerged.

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:49.675 align:start size:88% position:13%
In any case, I think
the most important thing

00:11:49.675 --> 00:11:53.612
for all of us to do right now
is find that center ground.

00:11:54.847 --> 00:11:57.049 align:start size:84% position:16%
Talk to people who
are on the center-left

00:11:57.049 --> 00:12:01.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
or on the center-right, and
make this attempt, once again,

00:12:03.055 --> 00:12:06.392 align:start size:88% position:13%
to marginalize the
fringes and extremists.

00:12:06.392 --> 00:12:10.496
And in that sense,
