00:47:57.274 --> 00:47:59.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's the unintended
message, maybe,

00:47:59.843 --> 00:48:01.478 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you are
conveying, and yeah,

00:48:01.478 --> 00:48:06.016 align:start size:97% position:3%
I would say a lot had to do
with, when it comes to Brexit,

00:48:06.016 --> 00:48:11.021 align:start size:97% position:3%
a lot had to do with that
tone-deaf attitude to Islam,

00:48:11.955 --> 00:48:13.957
immigration, the
clash of values.

00:48:15.292 --> 00:48:19.897 align:start position:0%
Same with countries like
Hungary, Europe, sorry, Poland,

00:48:21.298 --> 00:48:23.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
some of these Eastern European
countries that have taken

00:48:23.066 --> 00:48:25.769
on a harder line
toward immigration.

00:48:25.769 --> 00:48:29.873
I think a lot of it has
to do with them feeling

00:48:29.873 --> 00:48:32.576
that the leadership of the
core of the European project

00:48:32.576 --> 00:48:34.244
are just not listening to them.

00:48:34.244 --> 00:48:35.712
They're full of-

00:48:35.712 --> 00:48:37.114 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So do you, yeah, do you
think that places like Poland

00:48:37.114 --> 00:48:39.082
and Hungary are just
much better suited,

00:48:39.082 --> 00:48:41.652 align:start size:84% position:16%
at this point, to
survive all of this?

00:48:42.653 --> 00:48:43.587
Because of that?

00:48:45.522 --> 00:48:46.990
- I think it depends on

00:48:46.990 --> 00:48:49.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether they feel that
they're being listened to,

00:48:49.192 --> 00:48:52.095
and that they're not
being condescended to.

00:48:52.095 --> 00:48:54.431
It's the same experience
we had here in America

00:48:54.431 --> 00:48:58.168
where a lot of people
voted for Donald Trump

00:48:58.168 --> 00:49:02.339
because they felt that they
were being condescended to,

00:49:02.339 --> 00:49:07.244
that the establishment
had contempt for them,

00:49:07.244 --> 00:49:08.845
and only contempt.

00:49:08.845 --> 00:49:11.748
And there are a lot
of people in Europe,

00:49:11.748 --> 00:49:13.984
some small countries,
some bigger countries,

00:49:13.984 --> 00:49:16.753
who are saying you know,
"These people in Brussels,

00:49:16.753 --> 00:49:19.089
"they don't see us as
fellow human beings.

00:49:19.089 --> 00:49:22.359 align:start size:88% position:13%
"They call us parasites
in xenophobia.

00:49:22.359 --> 00:49:24.528
"They don't see our problems.

00:49:24.528 --> 00:49:25.996
"They're full of
contempt for us."

00:49:25.996 --> 00:49:29.800
And that obviously leads,
if you're a democracy,

00:49:31.268 --> 00:49:33.170 align:start size:97% position:3%
at the end of the day,
you're going to have to rely

00:49:33.170 --> 00:49:38.175 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the by-in, the votes,
you know, electoral victory.

00:49:39.409 --> 00:49:41.845 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then you'd better
listen to the people

00:49:41.845 --> 00:49:45.215
that you want to give you power.

00:49:45.215 --> 00:49:47.250 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So that's actually a
perfect segue to part four,

00:49:47.250 --> 00:49:52.189 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is "Solutions
Fake and Real."

00:49:52.189 --> 00:49:54.157
So what are some of
the fake solutions,

00:49:54.157 --> 00:49:57.094 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause I feel like those are
the ones that'll probably

00:49:57.094 --> 00:49:59.596
end up being used,
at least for a while.

00:50:02.833 --> 00:50:07.838
- One fake solution is that
this web, very complex web

00:50:10.107 --> 00:50:15.112 align:start position:0%
of legislation, rules, agencies,
that governs immigration

00:50:16.546 --> 00:50:21.251
in Europe, that that is to
be maintained going forward.

00:50:23.153 --> 00:50:24.187
That's a fixed solution.

00:50:24.187 --> 00:50:25.822
It has failed.

00:50:25.822 --> 00:50:28.959
The asylum and refugee system,

00:50:28.959 --> 00:50:31.528 align:start size:97% position:3%
the immigration system that
these countries have in place,

00:50:31.528 --> 00:50:35.499
are too complex, full
of too many loopholes,

00:50:35.499 --> 00:50:37.467
too many special interests.

00:50:37.467 --> 00:50:38.969
And when I talk about
special interests,

00:50:38.969 --> 00:50:41.571
I'm not only talking about the

00:50:44.374 --> 00:50:48.278
legitimate special interests
that lobby these governments.

00:50:48.278 --> 00:50:50.914 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm also talking about
people smugglers,

00:50:50.914 --> 00:50:52.482
and human traffickers.

00:50:52.482 --> 00:50:56.086
So there're just too
many, it's too complex.

00:50:56.086 --> 00:50:57.521
And so we have to go and review

00:50:57.521 --> 00:50:59.456
and revisit that that's a fake.

00:50:59.456 --> 00:51:04.161
So to carry on saying why
don't we make a distinction

00:51:05.729 --> 00:51:07.898 align:start size:84% position:16%
between those
qualify for asylum,

00:51:07.898 --> 00:51:09.866
and those who don't
qualify for asylum,

00:51:10.801 --> 00:51:13.737
I think that is totally,

00:51:15.672 --> 00:51:17.574
that that has failed.

00:51:17.574 --> 00:51:19.309 align:start size:88% position:13%
People who keep pushing
that are actually

00:51:19.309 --> 00:51:22.112
really pushing their
special interests.

00:51:22.112 --> 00:51:27.117
I think the second fake
approach would be to say,

00:51:29.619 --> 00:51:31.688 align:start size:88% position:13%
you take a bunch of
people in your country,

00:51:31.688 --> 00:51:33.924 line:0%
and I'll take a bunch
of people, and so on.

00:51:35.092 --> 00:51:39.129 line:0%
The reason why that is
fake is how many people

00:51:39.129 --> 00:51:42.332 align:start size:97% position:3%
could a country like Denmark
take, or even Germany,

00:51:42.332 --> 00:51:44.401
even the bigger countries?

00:51:44.401 --> 00:51:47.270
That would be like
a drop in the ocean

00:51:47.270 --> 00:51:51.875 align:start size:97% position:3%
when it comes to the displaced
peoples in the world.

00:51:51.875 --> 00:51:54.044
In fact, I was reading
a UN report yesterday

00:51:54.044 --> 00:51:57.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
that said 70% of the
people who end up

00:51:57.848 --> 00:52:00.450 align:start size:84% position:16%
on the shores of
Europe seeking asylum

00:52:00.450 --> 00:52:02.319
will not be granted asylum.

00:52:02.319 --> 00:52:03.253
They don't all.

00:52:03.253 --> 00:52:04.254
Seventy percent.

00:52:05.422 --> 00:52:08.625
And you know what, the
pandemic is gonna cause

00:52:08.625 --> 00:52:10.393
food shortages.

00:52:10.393 --> 00:52:12.796
Because of food shortages
there'll be more conflict.

00:52:12.796 --> 00:52:14.965 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because of conflict, there'll
be more displaced people.

00:52:14.965 --> 00:52:18.568
So the trend of the
millions of people

00:52:18.568 --> 00:52:20.303
who are trying to
get into Europe,

00:52:20.303 --> 00:52:21.571
that's not going to go down.

00:52:21.571 --> 00:52:23.507
That's only going
to go up, up, up.

00:52:23.507 --> 00:52:26.009
So what, then, would
be the real solution,

00:52:26.009 --> 00:52:28.111
and that would be to have
a serious conversation

00:52:28.111 --> 00:52:30.580
about push and pull factors.

00:52:30.580 --> 00:52:32.082
And you look at
the push factors,

00:52:32.082 --> 00:52:34.818
and the only way to really
deal seriously with that

00:52:34.818 --> 00:52:39.322
is through a collaboration
of these various countries.

00:52:39.322 --> 00:52:42.225
And that would have to be
let's break down the silos

00:52:42.225 --> 00:52:45.428
between the foreign
affairs departments,

00:52:45.428 --> 00:52:48.698
the defense departments, the
development aid departments,

00:52:48.698 --> 00:52:51.134
the economic affairs department.

00:52:51.134 --> 00:52:53.870
You break all that down and
you have to then figure out

00:52:55.305 --> 00:52:58.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
a more sort of, I would
say, I'm getting tired now,

00:52:58.808 --> 00:53:03.713
but it's like a big picture
approach sort of in ways

00:53:05.148 --> 00:53:08.451
equal to what we're doing
about the pandemic now.

00:53:08.451 --> 00:53:11.988
We're forcing a lot of
countries to collaborate

00:53:11.988 --> 00:53:15.492
on compromising their economies,

00:53:15.492 --> 00:53:20.130
or sacrificing the freedoms
of their populations to say

00:53:20.130 --> 00:53:22.032 align:start size:84% position:16%
let's get this
thing under control.

00:53:22.032 --> 00:53:25.135 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that kind of
approach would be appropriate

00:53:25.135 --> 00:53:26.836
for the immigration.

00:53:26.836 --> 00:53:28.038
And it's not immigration.

00:53:28.038 --> 00:53:29.973 align:start size:84% position:16%
Immigration is the
wrong word to use here

00:53:29.973 --> 00:53:33.243 align:start size:84% position:16%
for this mass
movement of people.

00:53:33.243 --> 00:53:36.680
- So one more for you, which I
think will sum up everything.

00:53:36.680 --> 00:53:38.014
Are you hopeful?

00:53:38.014 --> 00:53:41.084
Are you hopeful for the
world at the moment?

00:53:41.084 --> 00:53:42.852 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think a lot of people
are very fearful,

00:53:42.852 --> 00:53:44.888
and I've been trying
on my show every day

00:53:44.888 --> 00:53:48.892
to show them that you can't
just be dominated by fear.

00:53:48.892 --> 00:53:50.694 align:start size:81% position:19%
You have to be
dominated by hope.

00:53:50.694 --> 00:53:53.129
Your life story is
a story of hope.

00:53:53.129 --> 00:53:55.232 align:start size:81% position:19%
Are you hopeful
that we can solve,

00:53:55.232 --> 00:53:56.733
not only what we're
talking about here,

00:53:56.733 --> 00:53:59.402
but just sort of all
of the giant issues

00:53:59.402 --> 00:54:01.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
that seem to be
confronting us right now?

00:54:02.839 --> 00:54:05.208 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And you know, when
you say giants, you know

00:54:05.208 --> 00:54:06.409
think back about it.

00:54:06.409 --> 00:54:09.179
It's not even so
giant right now.

00:54:09.179 --> 00:54:11.214
Remember when America
was about to break up

00:54:11.214 --> 00:54:13.583 align:start size:84% position:16%
because there were
people who had slaves,

00:54:13.583 --> 00:54:18.021
and people who wanted
to go to war to end it.

00:54:18.021 --> 00:54:19.589
That was a giant issue.

00:54:20.957 --> 00:54:23.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
The slave trade all
across the world back then

00:54:23.860 --> 00:54:27.197 align:start size:88% position:13%
was one of the most
profitable enterprises,

00:54:27.197 --> 00:54:29.432
and we were able to end it.

00:54:31.501 --> 00:54:33.503
We fought two world wars,

00:54:34.771 --> 00:54:37.874 align:start size:84% position:16%
and human beings
were able to recover.

00:54:37.874 --> 00:54:39.743 align:start size:84% position:16%
There are all sorts
of places in the world

00:54:39.743 --> 00:54:43.113
where all sorts of conflicts
are going on at the moment.

00:54:43.113 --> 00:54:46.683
And people are able to
get out of it, recover,

00:54:46.683 --> 00:54:48.885
and leave something better
for the next generation.

00:54:48.885 --> 00:54:53.056
So I am hopeful now that
we're really in a place

00:54:53.056 --> 00:54:56.926 align:start size:81% position:19%
where science,
technology, money.

00:54:58.328 --> 00:55:00.363
We have so much money.

00:55:00.363 --> 00:55:02.899
I think if we put all
of those resources

00:55:02.899 --> 00:55:05.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have the largest
number of educated people.

00:55:05.268 --> 00:55:07.704
When I say educated,
I mean literate people

00:55:07.704 --> 00:55:09.172
who can read and write.

00:55:09.172 --> 00:55:12.275 align:start size:97% position:3%
My grandmother and my mother
could not read or write.

00:55:12.275 --> 00:55:16.780 align:start size:97% position:3%
So in the modern world, we
have just so much to work with

00:55:16.780 --> 00:55:18.448
to make things better

00:55:20.784 --> 00:55:22.285
But do we want to do it?

00:55:22.285 --> 00:55:23.586
It's the political will.

00:55:26.323 --> 00:55:29.526
And that we, people
like you and me,

00:55:29.526 --> 00:55:32.028 align:start size:84% position:16%
we just have to
keep harping on it.

00:55:32.028 --> 00:55:34.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I have nothing
better to do, do you?

00:55:35.298 --> 00:55:36.733
- No, no.

00:55:38.068 --> 00:55:41.237 align:start size:97% position:3%
So between fighting
radical Islam and woke-ism.

00:55:41.237 --> 00:55:43.740 align:start size:97% position:3%
- All right, we got our work
cut out for us, I guess.

00:55:43.740 --> 00:55:44.674
(audio cuts out)

00:55:44.674 --> 00:55:46.543
Well, the book is "Prey."

00:55:46.543 --> 00:55:48.578
The link is right down below,

00:55:48.578 --> 00:55:51.181 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it's just great
to see you, as always,

00:55:51.181 --> 00:55:55.085
and hopefully in person
next time, my friend.

00:55:56.619 --> 00:55:58.088
- In person next time.

00:55:58.088 --> 00:56:00.123 align:start size:97% position:3%
Thank you so much again
for everything that you do.

00:56:00.123 --> 00:56:01.358
